WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.350
All right, let's get into audience questions,
first question, David.

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:04.690
Why have the opposite?

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:11.559
Why has opposition to covid guidelines been
primarily a right wing thing in the United

00:00:11.559 --> 00:00:12.559
States?

00:00:12.559 --> 00:00:14.150
The in the United States is interesting.

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:18.350
I don't know if opposition in other countries
has been from the political right or not.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:22.460
There has been some covid guideline opposition
from the left.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:29.580
There are some I think there's a subset it
called like Liberal Lockdown's Skeptic's or

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:31.350
something along those lines.

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:34.690
But you're absolutely right that it's been
mostly from the political right.

00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:37.210
And I think there's a couple of different
things going on.

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:44.090
First of all, there is this sort of cartoonish
idea of liberty and freedom that exists on

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:47.989
the right, more so than it does on the left.

00:00:47.989 --> 00:00:52.690
And it's not that the left doesn't believe
in liberty and freedom, but the left has a

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:55.239
less cartoonish concept of what that means.

00:00:55.239 --> 00:01:01.399
So, for example, on the right, things like
liberty and freedom are often assigned to

00:01:01.399 --> 00:01:07.670
I can disregard anyone else's public health
concerns and do whatever the hell I want.

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:10.799
That's freedom and liberty on the right.

00:01:10.799 --> 00:01:16.759
On the left, we tend to see freedom and liberty
more as we have the freedom and liberty to

00:01:16.759 --> 00:01:24.969
live our lives, working wherever we find it,
to be most rewarding without having to consider

00:01:24.969 --> 00:01:28.469
whether we will have health insurance at this
job versus that job.

00:01:28.469 --> 00:01:30.920
That's the kind of freedom and liberty we
talk about on the left.

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:35.919
So obviously that right wing concept of freedom
and liberty is going to lead people down the

00:01:35.919 --> 00:01:42.259
path of needing to wear masks, businesses,
restaurants, having to be take out only.

00:01:42.259 --> 00:01:43.259
No, no, no.

00:01:43.259 --> 00:01:45.719
That's violating my my freedom and liberty.

00:01:45.719 --> 00:01:48.679
The other thing was certainly Trump related.

00:01:48.679 --> 00:01:55.989
And what I mean by that is Trump did nothing
early and Trump didn't wear masks.

00:01:55.989 --> 00:02:02.200
And Trump was skeptical of what was being
done in different in different parts of the

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:05.099
country with regard to certain governors and
so on and so forth.

00:02:05.099 --> 00:02:11.909
So by definition, what Trump wanted was seeing
as seen as the thing for freedom and what

00:02:11.909 --> 00:02:16.650
anybody else wanted was seen seen as a restriction
on so-called freedoms.

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:20.819
If you were suggesting something other than
what Trump was suggesting or doing importantly,

00:02:20.819 --> 00:02:25.129
then you were the enemy and it was bad and
you were restricting people's freedoms.

00:02:25.129 --> 00:02:32.680
Since coronavirus began during the Trump presidency
in an election year, there was this understanding

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:38.990
that anybody suggesting something be done
differently than what Trump wanted was essentially

00:02:38.990 --> 00:02:43.620
an indictment of Trump's response, which of
course required much indictment.

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:47.939
It was one of the worst five responses in
the world, according to it, to a recent study.

00:02:47.939 --> 00:02:53.120
And what continues to get me about that, even
now with Donald Trump gone, is that as much

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:59.890
as the virus handling was Trump's undoing,
it could have guaranteed his reelection.

00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:02.140
It was a wasted opportunity.

00:03:02.140 --> 00:03:07.400
Trump and the Republican Party, all they had
to do was stand aside and say, what are the

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:08.400
experts say?

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.360
Oh, they say masks.

00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:13.920
We're printing American flag masks.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.740
We want to get them out to everybody.

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:20.450
Instead of rejecting the idea of having the
Postal Service distribute masks to everybody,

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:24.420
they don't have to guess the postal service
will be bringing everybody five American flag

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:26.810
masks is the patriotic thing to do.

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:32.660
They could have passed, you know, they could
pass what they passed and more to serve as

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:35.159
a bridge to dealing with the virus.

00:03:35.159 --> 00:03:39.099
And Trump would have sailed to reelection
and Republicans likely would still control

00:03:39.099 --> 00:03:40.099
the Senate.

00:03:40.099 --> 00:03:45.459
So the the idea that it had to go the way
it went down, political lines with the anti

00:03:45.459 --> 00:03:51.299
maskers and the anti closures and guidelines,
people saying they are violating our freedom,

00:03:51.299 --> 00:03:55.590
they are treading on us and so on because
of the tone that was set by Trump that was

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:57.489
all optional.

00:03:57.489 --> 00:04:02.150
However, for Trump to have handled it differently
would have required Trump to be a different

00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:03.150
person.

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:09.379
The exact same narcissistic tendencies that
are what a lot of people were drawn to Trump

00:04:09.379 --> 00:04:15.180
by were what prevented Donald Trump from doing
what I suggested from the beginning, which

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:19.569
is saying, let's do what the doctors say,
let's be patriots.

00:04:19.569 --> 00:04:23.319
It'll be tough, but we're all going to do
it together.

00:04:23.319 --> 00:04:28.889
If Trump had had sort of bought into that,
he wouldn't have been Trump in a sense.

00:04:28.889 --> 00:04:30.920
And that's part of why he was unable to do
it.

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:33.300
I do think Trump's base would have followed
him.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:37.510
I got a few emails saying, you know, if Trump
had done this stuff, you're suggesting his

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:39.940
base wouldn't have followed him.

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:45.380
I think that Trump's base was more than willing
to be led in absolutely any direction at any

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:47.430
point in time.

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:51.601
And it was, listen, Trump would have had a
second term had he dealt with it properly.

